{"chapter": "desirables", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02BE", "placeholders": {"LATIN_0001": "\\'etale", "REF_0001": "\\ref{coherent-section-introduction}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{perfect-section-introduction}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{duality-section-introduction}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dfe180b0fa4824d05a2ecd033012acc89982cd946415efb318d6342ed8261c68", "source_text": "There is already a chapter on cohomology of quasi-coherent sheaves, see Cohomology of Schemes, Section <REF_0001>. We have a chapter discussing the derived category of quasi-coherent sheaves on a scheme, see Derived Categories of Schemes, Section <REF_0002>. We have a chapter discussing duality for Noetherian schemes and relative duality for morphisms of schemes, see Duality for Schemes, Section <REF_0003>. We also have chapters on <LATIN_0001> cohomology of schemes and on crystalline cohomology of schemes. But most of the material in these chapters is very basic and a lot more could/should be added there.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c1f92972b12af2bfda6f1e354b1b8a062843b90a93bd43d098e50c7e816206f2", "unit_id": "tag:02BE:p001"}
